{"id": "EUVD-2026-105164", "enisaUuid": "92162906-9c20-3bb7-845b-bd1cc77de185", "description": "Modoboa before 2.8.0 contains an insecure direct object reference vulnerability that allows authenticated users to delete alarms of other domains via the POST /api/v2/alarms/bulk_delete/ action. Attackers can enumerate sequential alarm IDs to delete DNS, MX and blocklist monitoring alarms server-wide, hiding problems from responsible administrators.", "datePublished": "2026-10-20T15:40:26", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T15:54:34", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/modoboa/modoboa/issues/3945", "https://github.com/modoboa/modoboa/commit/e0a4e3b9ee8ad84dba46e4c0f04cbbe7cf78c38d", "https://github.com/modoboa/modoboa/releases/tag/2.8.0", "https://github.com/modoboa/modoboa/blob/2.7.2/modoboa/admin/api/v2/viewsets.py", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/modoboa-before-2.8.0-idor-via-api-v2-alarms-bulk-delete"], "aliases": ["GHSA-cq85-78wv-p3mx", "CVE-2026-113598"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.25, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "46290aa1-ea60-3d85-ad31-2e36db202ab4", "product": {"name": "modoboa", "vendor": {"name": "modoboa"}}, "product_version": "0 <2.8.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "e9abfd42-4d10-33b1-bb5c-8fc9026b1de2", "vendor": {"name": "modoboa"}}], "isExploited": false}